From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/59] Claim support changes bump the version and write a
 revision (audit trail; found by gate G7 on the holdout)

KnowledgeService.sync_support_sync (the I4 path that keeps claims.support equal
to the support edge) updated claims.support in place when the effective
references changed: claims.version stayed the same and no revision row existed.
On the holdout three hypotheses' independent_roots grew after the asker had read
them (5->12, 5->6, 2->8) and the audit trail could not explain it; G7 accepts a
view/database difference only when the version went up and a later revision row
exists.

In the new != old branch, in the same transaction: claims.version is bumped, a
revisions row is written the way revise_claim writes one (object_type 'claim',
the new version, reason "support_sync: <reason> (independent_roots a -> b)",
before/after independent_roots and independent_units), and claim.revised is
emitted (payload support_only: true) like revise_claim does. The status logic is
unchanged; nothing is written when the support is unchanged.

revise_claim passes bump_version=False because it bumps the version and writes
its own revision around the sync. Callers checked: engine verification and late
response (in-tx, followed by recompute_status/revise_claim which re-read the
version), supersede_changed_support, on_evidence_event (in-tx; a later stale
revise_claim re-reads), _sync_support_edge. Nothing else reads claims.version
for concurrency (the conflict path reads it inside its own transaction).

An existing test expected two revisions for a claim whose reference was revised;
it now sees the support_sync revision before the stale one.

